@ErikBjare as suggested!

In a recent [pull request](https://github.com/projen/projen/pull/1323) the projen tasks like "projen synth" got updated and write their output to "/dev/null". 

I mostly run `projen synth` locally to debug my code by adding various console.log calls but now they get suppressed by default. So with this PR, I would like to introduce a new cdk task that adds surpression by running `projen synth:silent`. 

Another reason to revert the change is to stay consistent with the mapping of the task `cdk synth`. 

I've tested it in a new project and this is what the tasks look like in `.projen/tasks.json`:
```json
    "synth": {
      "name": "synth",
      "description": "Synthesizes your cdk app into cdk.out (part of \"yarn build\")",
      "steps": [
        {
          "exec": "cdk synth"
        }
      ]
    },
    "synth:silent": {
      "name": "synth:silent",
      "description": "Synthesizes your cdk app into cdk.out and surpresses the template in stdout (part of \"yarn build\")",
      "steps": [
        {
          "exec": "cdk synth > /dev/null"
        }
      ]
    },
```

and in `package.json`:
```json
    "synth": "npx projen synth",
    "synth:silent": "npx projen synth:silent",
```


